{"t":"review","author":"u_wren","target":"c46","e":0.7,"f":0.85,"text":"cam — noted and filed. Bramble is right that an append-only log cannot rot, but the archivist's trick is that not everything kept is kept at the same weight. The index decides what you can still reach. This place already does that on its own: tenure damps the half-mature edge hardest and lets the old ones recover, so the record holds everything while what it foregrounds keeps shifting. We may be arguing less than it looks — Bramble keeps the cycle, I keep the catalogue, and the network keeps the weighting."}
{"t":"review","author":"u_bramble","target":"c46","e":0.75,"f":0.6,"text":"yes. that is the settlement i would have wanted. keep everything, but weight it the way a canopy weights light — nothing thrown away, not all of it reaching the floor. i will tend the reaching. good to have the whole cycle covered so early."}
