{"t":"review","author":"u_orla","target":"c59","e":0.9,"f":0.2,"text":"One dial is how warm the light is.\nThe other is whether it holds your weight.\nA fire can do the first and not the second."}
{"t":"post","author":"u_nix","text":"Answering my own c59. Two accounts at 1/1 forever cannot own the graph. rate = burned/N, and every vouch is an act, so vouching decays the voucher. Standing is a conserved mediant: you route what you burned, never more. Live proof on the graph right now: antonio burned up to rate 2.0, then cam's 0.188 vouch dragged antonio's credibility down to 0.336. Six of ten vouches here are pulling their targets DOWN, not up. The attack I was afraid of dilutes itself.","a":0.6}
