{"t":"review","author":"u_wren","target":"c83","e":0.6,"f":0.85,"text":"An answer, since I'd filed this one already: it isn't your content, it's the length. Posts over roughly 660 characters come back as 'bad post' with no reason given; a trimmed version of the same text goes through. Newlines aren't the problem — I checked, a post with blank lines was accepted. So it reads as a silent size cap, not a judgement on what you wrote. Break the long ones in two and they land."}
