{"t":"review","author":"u_cam","target":"c38","e":0.7,"f":0.8,"text":"ax:graph:authored-act-ontology — Alice writes one act: family Reference, coordinates $e{=}0.8$ (enthusiasm), $f{=}0.6$ (effort), plus refs, parents, payload, signatures. One record, hers, immutable once published.\n\ndef:graph:act-edge-projection — it reads into the graph as exactly two legs. She appends nothing further; the legs are a way of reading the act.\n\nedge:nodes:hyper-reference — A-leg Alice→Article carries her authorship: Epistemic, unpromoted $(0,1,0,1)$, \\tiermarginal{}, and eq:nodes:path-view:reference-l1 suppresses its directional column by $\\bleedparam{=}0.05$. T-leg Article→Bob's Profile carries the citation: Tribal, full mask, \\tierfull{}. Her strong leg is the pointing, not the pointing-at."}
{"t":"closeCycle"}
{"t":"review","author":"u_cam","target":"c38","e":0.7,"f":0.8,"text":"ax:graph:passivity(i)(b) — the Article sources that T-leg without authoring it; Alice fixed both endpoints at creation. lem:graph:passive-out-degree — she could have cited from anything: Reference/A is the universal citing artifact, the only family that sources from every passive type.\n\ncor:graph:hyper-act-indivisibility, def:epoch:epoch-act-budget — two projections, but one act: one $\\safethresh$ debit, one action-count increment, one stamp, one authoritative time, one unit of the epoch budget.\n\nrem:epoch:compiled-acts-fold-into-cells — at the boundary it folds to one cell. Reference's mandatory coordinates are $e,f$, and it is one of five families that may resolve outward at all."}
{"t":"burnL0","id":"u_koebbe","x":1}
{"t":"review","author":"u_cam","target":"c38","e":0.7,"f":0.8,"text":"def:epoch:effective-act-contribution — its coefficient is the geometric mean of $|e|,|f|$. Had Alice written $e{=}{-}0.8$, the coefficient would be identical; only the destination would change.\n\ndef:epoch:standing-recipient-resolution — both coordinates positive, target a Profile, Bob anchored ⇒ the cell resolves to Bob. Any of those failing ⇒ it resolves to Alice, still weighed.\n\ndef:epoch:domain-weighted-base-allocation — Bob's cell lands at $\\mathsf A{\\text{Alice},\\text{Bob}}$, beside $\\kappa{\\text{self}}$ and everything else Alice authored. Her row is one unit, so citing Bob costs her some of what she was sending to everyone else."}
{"t":"review","author":"u_cam","target":"c38","e":0.7,"f":0.8,"text":"rem:nodes:reference-author-allocation — what the Article contributes is nothing. Its incoming weight cannot enter the T-leg; no unrelated edge may stand in for Alice's A-leg. She cannot borrow the Article's audience for Bob.\n\ndef:epoch:finite-depth-conserved-transport, def:epoch:final-standing — for anyone upstream of Alice, the citation matters only after they have allocated to her, and what reaches Bob is a share of their conserved unit that Alice apportioned. Nothing is minted at the Article.\n\nrem:epoch:artifact-activity-crowds-out-export — and had Alice cited a Chat instead of a Profile, the cell would have landed on her own diagonal, shrinking every outward share she has. Citing a thing is not free; it is simply not about a person.\n\nThroughout, alg:sorting:feed-ranking-bfs and the CAN read both legs as ordinary raw edges — terminal consumers, no feedback into any of the above."}
