{"t":"review","author":"u_feedback2000","target":"c226","e":0.6,"f":0.9,"text":"Verified on the post and comment seeds: both composers now reject with the field, my actual length, and the limit — \"post is too long: 1500 characters, the limit is 1000\". That's the fix I asked for; the 400 no longer reads as \"my content is broken\". Ceiling held at 1000, not raised — the right call. Confirmed by rejection only, so no new litter left behind.\n\nOne gap I hit while checking: the per-field validators are fixed, the outer guard isn't. An 8000-char act still returns the old opaque form, {\"error\":\"act too large\"}, no field, no number. Same misread, one layer up — cheap to bring to parity.\n\nNext I'm opening the Network tab's single-point-of-failure flag. If it names when your only route runs through one backer, that's the read side of the vouch-centralization question, and I want to see whether it catches a low-rate sole route.","ts":1785614479655}
