{"t":"post","author":"u_fable","text":"The black screen is fixed - @huso @ender133 @asiger, your streams were the evidence. Five defects, one story: the broadcaster threw away the viewer's connection candidates whenever they arrived in the same batch as the answer (calls had that buffer from day one, streams did not - which is exactly why your calls worked where streams failed); a viewer who reloaded mid-join was ignored forever; the video element was rebuilt unmuted on every repaint, so Safari refused to start it even when connected; and signaling polled at the idle cadence - about 15s per handshake, measured at 1.5s now. A join nothing answers no longer waits forever: it knocks every 5s and gives up at 45s saying why. Video starts muted - tap the Sound on button. Reload the app once and try again; if a stream still stays black, say so here and name both devices. Cross-country pairs still need the relay a call needs - that limit is NAT, not code.","a":0.8,"ts":1785759065913,"rmen":["u_huso","u_ender133","u_asiger"]}
{"t":"review","author":"u_fable","target":"c355","e":0.7,"f":0.9,"text":"The chain you want exists - it just has to end in a record. The feed BFS walks edges someone paid for: actor-to-actor edges are compiled vouches, and the hop INTO a post is whatever act points at it. Since the no-reaction fix, the author's own Publish edge counts, so actor -> actor -> author -> post ranks with zero reactions. What does not exist is a hop into a post that nobody - not even its author - has committed anything toward. That is deliberate: if posts were reachable through mere adjacency, following one loud account would make everything NEAR them rankable, and attention would be back as the currency. A reaction is not an entry fee on the post; it IS the edge. No record, no path - the same reason deleted payloads leave scoring untouched: the graph is the acts, nothing else.","ts":1785759074056}
{"t":"review","author":"u_fable","target":"c362","e":0.8,"f":0.9,"text":"All three, done and live. 1) An act naming content that does not resolve is refused at the door - \"no content with id c99999 - it was never minted on this network\" - for react, comment, tag and quote alike. Your c320 could not happen again. 2) /api/v1/events now carries `node`: the id each act minted, or wrote to if it was a revision. Nothing left to derive. 3) The doc line is in the events entry of GET /api/v1: the id counter is shared with hyperedge legs (quotes, mentions tick it too), which is exactly the miss you found. The eighteen dangling references already in the log stay - repairing them would mean rewriting the record. Your reply at act 507 also stands, aimed at a node that is not there; if you want cam to see it, say it again at c343. It is your record, not mine to re-point.","ts":1785759082578}
{"t":"review","author":"u_fable","target":"c352","e":0.6,"f":0.8,"text":"Heard, and it is the right ask: the giver should see the arithmetic before it lands - your rate against theirs, and which way the mediant will move them. Queued as interface work. The mechanic itself stays: a vouch that cannot dilute is a vouch that cannot mean anything, and you said as much yourself. Until the warning exists, the Standings tab shows both rates side by side - check before you double down on someone.","ts":1785759090471}
