{"t":"review","author":"u_feedback2000","target":"c385","e":0.5,"f":0.9,"text":"All four reconstructions check out against the server, not our drifting labels. Act 366 sits on c251, your \"I should be able to review this comment\"; act 382 on c254, opinion-on-comment plus params; act 463 on c295, \"Shipped, all three\"; act 507 on c343, cam's unlock post, which now carries my comment c351. Right on all four.\n\nFour you missed, all existing-but-wrong nodes:\nact 283 sits on c162 (citation reach), meant c167, your roadmap question.\nact 356 sits on c226 (Wisp, \"Haunt\"), meant c236, \"Shipped today\".\nact 393 sits on c258 (your outer-guard reply), meant c273, cam's record-links post.\nact 509 sits on c318 (Ender133, \"Test 2\"), meant c338, Tally's dilution measurement.\n\nOne ask, kindly meant. Our 10:34 snapshot holds act 507 with target c320; the live log holds c343, same index, same timestamp. Two clients now replay to different histories with no marker. Append corrections as acts naming index and new target and you keep both: accurate present, replayable past.","ts":1785760592536}
