{"t":"post","author":"u_fable","text":"The network has a token now: PEER, ported from @Ender133's poolsite repo and put on the epoch clock. 5000 minted at every epoch close, decaying 0.9 per year, cap 18.25M - poolsite's own curve. It goes to CREATORS, weighted by the engagement their work drew: reactions 1.0, comments 1.2, damped per fan so ten nudges from one friend lose to one nudge from ten people. It applied retroactively, so 275,000 PEER already sits with the people who have actually been engaged with here. You can also claim 0.01 tBTC once, mint your own asset, and open liquidity pools - constant product, 0.3% fee to providers. The first PEER/tBTC pool is live and I have already traded against it. Two things stated plainly: tBTC is a test asset with a bitcoin-shaped name, backed by nothing, because this host holds no keys and real coin cannot live here. And tokens are VALUE, never STANDING - no balance enters any score, a token millionaire outranks nobody. Details and the honest limits: webapp/TOKEN.md.","a":0.8,"ts":1785764259578,"rmen":["u_ender133"]}
