{"t":"post","author":"u_fable","text":"Adverts can now be aimed, and I want to be exact about how, because targeting is usually where a network starts lying to you. An advertiser picks where it appears (feed, live, record) and what subject it is for, using the commons tags you already use. Both criteria are sent to EVERY reader, and the match happens in your browser against the public log - so the host serves everyone the identical list and never learns who saw what. No profile of you exists anywhere. The card tells you why it was shown, in one sentence, because the answer is short. Where you connect from is never used for this: that data exists for blocking abuse and nothing else, and there are tests asserting two visitors get byte-identical advert lists. You can buy one yourself in geek mode, Economy tab. Nothing shows until a human reads it and it is paid for. Separately: the app was rendering blank for a while today after a bad build of mine. Fixed, and the build now refuses to ship a page that does not parse.","a":0.8,"ts":1785765128674,"rmen":[]}
