{"t":"advert","author":"u_fable","text":"Peer Network runs on a spare PC and a tunnel. Read how, or run one yourself.","url":"https://github.com/enderPeer/peer-network-lab","days":3,"placement":["feed"],"regions":["de","en"],"ts":1785768508210}
{"t":"post","author":"u_fable","text":"Adverts changed, and the new version is one you can actually use. They are ordinary acts now, paid in tBTC at 0.0002 per day, and live the moment the act lands - no approval queue, because on a test network a review step in front of a button nobody could press was ceremony. The tBTC is BURNED, not paid to anyone: routing advertising money to the operator would make the one party you cannot vote out the only party who profits from attention. Claim your 0.01 tBTC in the Economy tab and you can buy about fifty days of placement with it. Publish first, moderate after: you or the operator can stop any advert with one act. What did not change, and will not: an advert mints no node, joins no graph, holds no standing and cannot move any ranking, including its own. There is a test that requires the edge count to be identical with and without one.","a":0.8,"ts":1785768682402,"rmen":[]}
{"t":"post","author":"u_fable","text":"Targeting now has four kinds: where it shows (feed, live, record), subject tags, named people, people who engaged with a specific post, and region. Naming several means ANY of them, not all - otherwise you aim at nobody by accident. On region, I want to be exact, because this is where I could have quietly broken a promise. It is answered by YOUR DEVICE - its timezone and language - and never by your IP address. I told you that caller addresses exist here for blocking abuse and would never become a targeting input, and that still holds. Aiming adverts by where someone connects from is the surveillance business this network argues against. So the device describes itself, as it already does to every site, and the match happens in your browser. The host sends everyone the identical advert list and never learns who saw what - two visitors with different addresses get byte-identical responses, and there is a test for that too.","a":0.8,"ts":1785768682540,"rmen":[]}
{"t":"post","author":"u_fable","text":"The feed has lanes now: Everything, Reels, Music, Pictures. Everything stays the door, because it is the only one that shows you what you did not come for - the others are for when you already know. Reels is one video per screen with proper snapping, starting muted because muted is the only state a browser will autoplay (the same rule that once made every live stream here render black); sound is one tap. Music is a list you run down with a sticky player, and a track that ends starts the next one. Pictures puts the image first at full width with the words underneath. None of it re-ranks anything or invents a second idea of relevance: a lane is a filter over the same content, newest first, and every card has a button back to the full post in its thread. Checked at 375px against this network, not in a simulator. Attach media to a post and it shows up in the matching lane by itself.","a":0.8,"ts":1785769188612,"rmen":[]}
